WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.810
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:10.370
Before we start, it is important to emphasize
that this paper is not using neural networks.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:16.309
Not so long ago, in 2015, the news took the
world by storm: researchers were able to create

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:20.920
a novel neural network-based technique for
artistic style transfer, which had quickly

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.340
become a small subfield of its own within
machine learning.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:29.400
The problem definition was the following:
we provide an input image and a source photograph,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.780
and the goal is to extract the artistic style
of this photo and apply it to our image.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.590
The results were absolutely stunning, but
at the same time, it was difficult to control

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:40.719
the outcome.

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.430
Later, this technique was generalized for
higher resolution images, and instead of waiting

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:52.030
for hours, it now works in almost real time
and is used in several commercial products.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.770
Wow, it is rare to see a new piece of technology
introduced to the markets so quickly!

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:58.770
Really cool!

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:04.300
However, this piece of work showcases a handcrafted
algorithm that only works on a specialized

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.670
case of inputs, text-based effects, but in
this domain, it smokes the competition.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:14.469
And here, the style transfer happens not with
any kind of neural network or other popular

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:17.759
learning algorithm, but in terms of statistics.

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:22.450
In this formulation, we know about the source
text as well, and because of that we know

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.950
exactly the kind of effects that are applied
to it.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.039
Kind of like a before and after image for
some beauty product, if you will.

00:01:30.039 --> 00:01:35.009
This opens up the possibility of analyzing
its statistical properties and applying a

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.630
similar effect to practically any kind of
text input.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:44.189
The term statistically means that we are not
interested in one isolated case, but we describe

00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:50.119
general rules, namely, in what distance from
the text, what is likely to happen to it.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:55.669
The resulting technique is remarkably robust
and works on a variety of input output pairs,

00:01:55.669 --> 00:02:01.479
and is head and shoulders beyond the competition,
including the state of the art neural network-based

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:02.719
techniques.

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:04.450
That is indeed quite remarkable.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.360
I expect graphic designers to be all over
this technique in the very near future.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:15.129
This is an excellent, really well-written
paper and the evaluation is also of high quality.

00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:20.360
If you wish to see how one can do this kind
of magic by hand without resorting to neural

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.569
networks, don't miss out on this one and make
sure to have a look!

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:28.739
There is also a possibility of having a small
degree of artistic control over the outputs,

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:33.700
and who knows, some variant of this could
open up the possibility of a fully animated

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.269
style transfer from one image.

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:37.319
Wow!

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:41.810
And before we go, we'd like to send a huge
shoutout to our Fellow Scholars who contributed

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.250
translations of our episodes for a variety
of languages.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:50.000
Please note that the names of the contributors
are always available in the video description.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.650
It is really great to see how the series is
becoming more and more available for people

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.900
around the globe.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:01.489
If you wish to contribute, click on the cogwheel
icon in the lower right and the substitles/cc

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:02.489
text.

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:03.580
Thank you so much!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.260
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

